      why: "【The classic, aristocratic glass】Lifted, grape-derived fruit and floral aromatics, together with barrel-aged vanilla, caramel, dried apricot, nuts, orange peel and rancio, entwine exquisitely with a cigar. Its smooth finish is said to shine especially in the final third, as the cigar's flavours intensify.\n【Reading the age statements】VS (2 years or more) is generally young and hard and considered unsuited to pairing; VSOP (4 years or more) is the entry point, and XO (10 years or more) the golden rule. That XO's deep complexity and velvet texture make the most rewarding match is the shared view of several sources.\n【Armagnac's character】Armagnac, distilled in a single pass, keeps more of the grape's individuality, and is wilder, earthier and more forceful than cognac. It keeps close company with aged, complex cigars and stands up well to full bodies. Cigar-dedicated blends such as Frapin's also exist.",
