      why: "【The non-alcoholic inner sanctum】Black tea's malty depth amplifies a cigar's earth and cacao notes. Robust Assam or Kenyan teas suit full cigars, while the lighter flavours of Darjeeling or oolong match a medium — that is the rough guide.\n【The Lapsang Souchong trick】Lapsang Souchong, smoked over pinewood, carries 'a smokiness reminiscent of a fine cigar' and is said to complement rather than compete with cigar smoke. An advanced move that resonates especially with smoky, Latakia-like cigars.\n【The delicacy of oolong and green tea】Semi-oxidised oolong has a creamy, biscuity sweetness and makes a surprisingly good partner for a cigar. Roasted oolongs such as Wuyi rock tea can handle fuller cigars too. Green tea is the most delicate of all, so keep it to milds and claros, and it is wise to avoid brewing it astringent.",
      ex: "Assam/Kenya → full. Darjeeling/oolong → medium. Lapsang Souchong / smoky Assam → smoky cigars. Green tea → mild, claro."
